Data Structures and Algorithms form the foundation of computer science and software engineering. Huffman coding is an optimal prefix code algorithm used for lossless data compression. Invented by David A. Huffman in 1952, it assigns variable-length codes to input characters based on their frequencies. More frequent characters receive shorter bit sequences, while less frequent characters receive longer bit sequences.
